# Merge policy

- `main` is the release trunk; keep it green.
- **Single-agent / single-domain PRs** → `main` when CI green — **unless** an active `/execute-plan` snapshot or an active **`/light-plan`** programme sets work onto an integration branch (see below).
- **Multi-agent sprints** → `cursor/sprint-<N>-<topic>-integration-13e3`; agents merge there; **one PR** to `main`. Use `/spawn-sprint-agents`.
- **`/light-plan`** — integration `cursor/<slug>-integration-<suffix>`; phase PRs merge-committed into integration via the skill's **light merge** (not **`/babysit-plus`**); **one release PR** integration → `main` via **`/babysit-uat`**. Do not catch that integration branch up to `main` unless the release conflicts. Agent merge for programme-owned PRs: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md) §Autonomy and merging. See [light-plan skill](../skills/light-plan/SKILL.md).
- **`/execute-plan` (2+ phases, `autonomy: active`)** — read `base_branch` from `.agents/plans/<plan_id>.snapshot.json` (usually `cursor/<plan_id>-integration-<suffix>`). **Phase PRs target `base_branch`, not `main`.** Squash-merge via **`/babysit-plus`** into integration; **one release PR** integration → `main` via **`/babysit-uat`**. Do not use the single-agent→`main` default for intermediate phase PRs.

## Before every push

1. On a dev or agent branch, `git fetch` its parent and rebase onto it (`origin/main`, or the integration branch).
2. On an integration branch (`cursor/*-integration-*`): do not rebase (`non_fast_forward`) and do not merge `main` in because the branch is behind. The release PR merges that branch into `main`. Squash-merge it when GitHub reports `MERGEABLE`, including when the state is `BEHIND`. Merge `main` into the integration branch only when that release is conflicted. Ruleset 18979034 must keep `strict_required_status_checks_policy` false so GitHub accepts that merge. A clean behind merge that GitHub rejects is that flag, not a conflict — do not open a sync PR.
3. `./scripts/pre-push-changed.sh` during work; `./scripts/pre-push.sh` before the release PR

`/execute-plan` still opens its own sync PR when the driver sees the integration branch behind `main` before release. Light-plan and babysit follow this section.

## Branch naming

- Integration (sprint): `cursor/sprint-<N>-<topic>-integration-13e3`
- Integration (execute-plan): `cursor/<plan_id>-integration-<suffix>` — snapshot `base_branch`
- Integration (light-plan): `cursor/<slug>-integration-<suffix>`; dev `cursor/<slug>-dev`
- Agent: `cursor/<descriptive-name>-13e3` or `cursor/<descriptive-name>-feec`

Full ownership matrix and anti-patterns: `.cursor/rules/agent-coordination.mdc` and `docs/agent-efficiency/plans/agent-efficiency-plan.md`.
